  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 255 PM EDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nOn Thursday, the front will practically stall over the region and \ncontinued convergence along the front will keep widespread showers \nand storms over the region. Later Thursday and into Friday, an upper \ntrough moves across the Ohio Valley and gives the surface front some \nsouthward momentum. At this time, showers and storms will cease over \nthe northern half of the region and remain over the southern half \nthrough Friday. \n\nBeyond Friday, the front will remain in the region and the upper \npattern will remain active with multiple shortwaves moving over the \nregion. Periods of showers and storms are expected through the \nweekend and into early next week. Ridging looks to build in from the \nsouth early next week, which will lead to warmer than normal \ntemperatures.",
